; AlgoX SuperTrend Pro EA - preset 00_Pine_Baseline
; Reference: the raw indicator signal
; family: reference | hard filters: none
; status: control
; The raw signal: original Pine weights (fib 25, structure 30, EMA 25, RSI 20), no MACD and no volume scoring, the original reference SL/TP and the original TP1 exit, with the cost gates switched off - but with the same account sizing and the same safety layer as every other preset, so the comparison is about the signal and not about broken sizing. Run it twice: once with the tester spread at 47 (the real cost) and once at 0 (does the raw signal have any edge at all?). The pair of results tells you whether the problem is the signal or the cost.
; Generated by generate_presets.py - do not edit by hand.
; Copy to MQL4/Presets and load it from the Inputs tab (Load button).
; Coherence rules: max 2 hard filters per family, max 5 in total,
; everything else inside a family stays on score so the filters do not fight each other.

